# The unclosed `(` is reported where it opens, even lines away from where the input ends.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv'
| where (amount > 10
| take 5
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..43
  PIPELINE@0..42
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 "\n"
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    WHERE_OP@15..42
      IDENT@15..20 "where"
      WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
      PAREN_EXPR@21..42
        L_PAREN@21..22 "("
        PIPELINE@22..42
          BIN_EXPR@22..33
            NAME_REF@22..28
              IDENT@22..28 "amount"
            WHITESPACE@28..29 " "
            GT@29..30 ">"
            WHITESPACE@30..31 " "
            LITERAL@31..33
              LONG@31..33 "10"
          WHITESPACE@33..34 "\n"
          PIPE@34..35 "|"
          WHITESPACE@35..36 " "
          TAKE_OP@36..42
            IDENT@36..40 "take"
            WHITESPACE@40..41 " "
            LITERAL@41..42
              LONG@41..42 "5"
  WHITESPACE@42..43 "\n"

error[DS0112]: unclosed `(`
  --> query:2:9
  |
2 | | where (amount > 10
  |         ^ this `(` is never closed
3 | | take 5
  |         - the input ends before a `)`
  |
  = help: add `)` where the bracketed part ends
